{"name":"April Showers","hex":"#dadeb5","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"showers","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of shower"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of shower"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/showers"}],"entries":[{"title":"April shower","blocks":[{"text":"In parts of the Northern Hemisphere, an April shower is rain during the month of April. One of the major causes of the often heavy downpours is the position of the jet stream. In early spring, the jet stream starts to move northwards, allowing large depressions to bring strong winds and rain in from the Atlantic. In one day the weather can change from springtime sunshine to winter sleet and snow. The track of these depressions can often be across Ireland and Scotland bringing bands of rain followed by heavy showers and strong blustery winds. In France, this meteorological phenomenon is known as \"Giboulées de mars\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Snow_shower_on_Dartmoor.jpg/330px-Snow_shower_on_Dartmoor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/April_shower"},{"title":"April Showers (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"April Showers\" is a 1921 popular song composed by Louis Silvers with lyrics by B. G. De Sylva."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/April_Showers.pdf/page1-250px-April_Showers.pdf.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/April_Showers_(song)"},{"title":"April Showers (1948 film)","blocks":[{"text":"April Showers is a 1948 American musical film directed by James V. Kern and written by Peter Milne. The film stars Jack Carson, Ann Sothern, Robert Alda, S. Z. Sakall, Robert Ellis and Richard Rober. The film was released by Warner Bros. on March 27, 1948."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/10/April_Showers_%281948_film%29_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/April_Showers_(1948_film)"},{"title":"April","blocks":[{"text":"April is the fourth month of the year in the Gregorian and Julian calendars. Its length is 30 days."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/April"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/April_Showers.pdf/page1-250px-April_Showers.pdf.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/April_Showers.pdf/page1-250px-April_Showers.pdf.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AApril_Showers.pdf"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Breviarium_Grimani_-_April.jpg/500px-Breviarium_Grimani_-_April.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Breviarium_Grimani_-_April.jpg/500px-Breviarium_Grimani_-_April.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"April, Brevarium Grimani, fol. 5v (Flemish)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABreviarium_Grimani_-_April.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/36/Diamond.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/36/Diamond.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Faceted diamond","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADiamond.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Daisy_ntgr.JPG/500px-Daisy_ntgr.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org